    "id": "richfrem/agent-plugins-skills/os-lab-planner",
    "name": "os-lab-planner",
    "description": "Turns a confirmed improvement brief into an evidence-based plan: audits what already exists, chooses a path (orchestrate existing, update existing, or create new), brainstorms 2-3 options with tradeoffs, then writes the task plan and a self-contained delegation prompt. Non-interactive: it works from the brief that os-lab-agent hands it and does not interview the user. Use when asked to \"plan an improvement\", \"write a delegation prompt\", \"audit what exists before improving X\", \"should we update or create this skill\", or when os-lab-agent has a confirmed brief. DO NOT USE to build the lab repo (os-lab-setup), run mutation iterations (os-lab-loop), score a change (os-lab-scorer), review or backport lab results (os-lab-backport), write run logs or charts (os-lab-log), or manage memory (os-lab-memory).\n",
